@page "/"

<PageTitle>Blazor Server Demo - Scoped Stores</PageTitle>

<div class="container mt-4">
    <h1>🔒 Blazor Server - Scoped Store Demo</h1>
    <p class="lead">Demonstrating per-user data isolation and Redux DevTools with scoped stores</p>

    <div class="alert alert-info mt-4">
        <h4 class="alert-heading">✨ What This Demo Shows</h4>
        <ul class="mb-0">
            <li><strong>Scoped Stores Work with DevTools!</strong> - Using IServiceProvider in configure callback</li>
            <li><strong>Per-User Isolation</strong> - Each SignalR circuit gets its own store instance</li>
            <li><strong>Proper Async Patterns</strong> - Cross-store updates using UpdateAsync</li>
            <li><strong>Singleton vs Scoped</strong> - Side-by-side comparison</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="row mt-4">
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <div class="card">
                <div class="card-header bg-danger text-white">
                    <h5 class="mb-0">⚠️ The Problem: Singleton Stores</h5>
                </div>
                <div class="card-body">
                    <p>In Blazor Server, singleton stores are <strong>shared across all users</strong>:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>❌ All clients see the same state</li>
                        <li>❌ User A's actions affect User B</li>
                        <li>❌ No data isolation</li>
                        <li>❌ Privacy concerns</li>
                    </ul>
                    <a href="singleton-counter" class="btn btn-danger">See the Problem →</a>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="col-md-6">
            <div class="card">
                <div class="card-header bg-success text-white">
                    <h5 class="mb-0">✅ The Solution: Scoped Stores</h5>
                </div>
                <div class="card-body">
                    <p>Scoped stores provide <strong>per-user isolation</strong>:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>✅ Each user gets their own instance</li>
                        <li>✅ Complete data isolation</li>
                        <li>✅ Privacy protected</li>
                        <li>✅ DevTools work!</li>
                    </ul>
                    <a href="scoped-counter" class="btn btn-success">See the Solution →</a>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card mt-4">
        <div class="card-header bg-primary text-white">
            <h5 class="mb-0">📚 Learn More</h5>
        </div>
        <div class="card-body">
            <h6>Key Discovery (Your Contribution!)</h6>
            <p>The breakthrough was adding <code>IServiceProvider</code> to the scoped store configure callback:</p>
            <pre class="bg-light p-3 rounded"><code>// ✅ This enables DevTools in Blazor Server with scoped stores!
builder.Services.AddScopedStore(
    new CounterState(0),
    (storeBuilder, sp) => storeBuilder.WithDevTools(sp, "Counter"));
</code></pre>

            <h6 class="mt-3">Navigation</h6>
            <ul>
                <li><a href="comparison">Store Comparison</a> - See both stores side-by-side</li>
                <li><a href="user-session">User Session</a> - Per-user session tracking</li>
                <li><a href="cross-store">Cross-Store Updates</a> - Proper async patterns</li>
            </ul>

            <div class="alert alert-warning mt-3">
                <strong>Open Redux DevTools!</strong> You'll see separate DevTools instances for each scoped store. Switch between them using the dropdown in DevTools.
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
